1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,296
屋檐，为什么能伸出去？
How can an eave reach beyond its columns?

2
00:00:08,296 --> 00:00:18,560
中国建筑之 ORDER
The Chinese “Order”

3
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:27,768
先看路径：屋面 → 斗拱 → 柱 → 柱础
Follow the load: roof → brackets → column → base

4
00:00:27,768 --> 00:00:37,744
斗与拱，像托盘与伸出的手臂
Blocks receive; arms reach outward

5
00:00:37,744 --> 00:00:48,704
20 栌斗：柱头上的承接节点
20 • Ludou: the receiving block above the column

6
00:00:48,704 --> 00:00:58,944
19 华拱：向外出跳的构件
19 • Huagong: an outward-reaching arm

7
00:00:58,944 --> 00:01:10,240
17 昂：图中斜向延伸的构件
17 • Ang: the inclined members in the drawing

8
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:21,752
这组斗拱：三跳 = 一华拱 + 两昂
Three projections = one huagong + two ang

9
00:01:21,752 --> 00:01:33,672
材：让构件尺寸互相协调的比例基准
Cai: a modular reference for coordinated dimensions

10
00:01:33,672 --> 00:01:45,400
上部：飞椽、檐椽与橑檐枋
Above: flying rafters, eave rafters and eave purlin

11
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:56,216
下部：柱、柱础与地栿
Below: column, base and ground-level tie

12
00:01:56,216 --> 00:02:09,072
ORDER：读懂构件之间的秩序
Order: reading the relationships between parts

13
00:02:09,072 --> 00:02:22,192
下次抬头看屋檐，你会看到结构
Next time you look up, you will see the structure
